  "term": "psychotherapy research",
  "definition": "Psychotherapy research is the study of psychotherapy interventions and their effects on therapeutic outcomes in different client groups. It also examines how clearly and rigorously studies are conducted and reported, and seeks to understand the specific processes that produce change in therapy.",
